{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/972282-enhancing-yourself-to-heal-like-a-garou","id":972282,"title":"Enhancing Yourself to \"heal like a garou\"","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-18T19:18:57-07:00","id":972282,"title":"Enhancing Yourself to \"heal like a garou\"","content":"I'd like to see how some of y'all would handle this from a player: <br /> <br /> He would like to, through Sphere magick, give his character the ability to regenerate damage &quot;like a werewolf.&quot; <br /> <br /> He has Life 4, Spirit 3, Prime 4.<br /> <br /> He has taken the heart from a garou and has been using it in his sanctum to try to figure some things out. He's come up with the idea of giving himself a second heart and he wants the following effect:<br /> <br /> Whenever hurt, heal one health level per round. (He also wants (eventually) to gain the &quot;revive recently dead&quot; power).<br /> <br /> <br /> Specific Questions:<br /> 1. What are the sphere effects you'd require for the above power? <br /> 2. Would you use the &quot;enhancement&quot; background to cover this (representing permanent modification to his pattern)?<br /> 3. Player is trying to argue that he shouldn't get permanent paradox, but instead it should generate paradox when healing...<br /> 4. What would you suggest for the mechanics of power like this?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> My take so far: <br /> <br /> I'm inclined to let the player do this, if only because I think it's a horrible idea. I told him we'd work on things... but I'm assuming that we'll start with creating a wonder and then making it a permanent change in his pattern.... (to figure out costs). I think this should then be handled through the Enhancement Background. <br /> <br /> It feels like, maybe, this power should require Time 4 as well... so that it only heals him when he's hurt...<br /> <br /> I'm considering letting him take Genetic Flaws instead of the Permadox. (I really don't like the idea of having this sort of power without a significant price (and not just in a dangerously difficult casting...)<br /> <br /> I'm also considering making him &quot;Wyrm Tainted.&quot; (It's mostly a Mage game, but there is significant interaction with Garou...)<br /> <br /> I'm also thinking that if he wants to heal Ag damage, then it would cost Quintessence per health level...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12296-gabryl","name":"Gabryl","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T19:51:56-07:00","id":972294,"title":"","content":"1.) Life 3 for healing. Life 5 if they want to avoid Pattern bleed.<br /> 2.) No. Enhancement background represents technocratic connections rather than just permanently modifying ones pattern.<br /> 3.) Sorry, that's the way modifying your pattern works. You get Permadox.<br /> 4.) *shrugs*<br /> <br /> If you're gonna do the wonder thing. Make it a Talisman. Use Prime 4 to have it bind to his pattern. In which case, yes, it would actually only generate paradox when it did it's thing. Though personally, I would do it as a permanent duration effect because wonders are broken as fuck.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I'm not looking at the book at the moment so I could be wrong... but...<br /> <br /> He would need 1 success per health level of healing. Then double that number for duration. You'd need Prime 3 IIRC to heal Agg but I don't THINK it cost quint. Unsure on that though.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T20:57:50-07:00","id":972320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gabryl</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/972282-enhancing-yourself-to-heal-like-a-garou#post972282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. What are the sphere effects you'd require for the above power?</div> </div> </div> </div>Life 4/Prime 4 probably ought to cut it if he has the Tass (Werewolves are an excellent form of Tass for this). Nanotech Integration does that and more, and only has a single dot higher of Prime and some Matter; given it seems to use 'is really expensive' as a source of Quint, lowering it to Life 4/Prime 4 but requiring Tass rather than free Quintessence seems legit.<br /> <br /> I don't really see Time as being pertinent since it'll already heal him only when he's hurt.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. Would you use the &quot;enhancement&quot; background to cover this (representing permanent modification to his pattern)? </div> </div> </div>Probably yes. Or Revised-style Blessing which is &quot;Enhancements for Traditions&quot;. Or a Xenograft (see Progenitors Revised for examples). Sounds like... 3 Device points' worth, as a first guess? So 6xp and a point of Permadox.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. Player is trying to argue that he shouldn't get permanent paradox, but instead it should generate paradox when healing... </div> </div> </div>That is <i>adorable</i>.<br /> <br /> But no, he gets his augs and he takes his 'dox. Or Genetic Flaws, either way. Make 'em appropriately wolfy!<br /> <br /> If he doesn't want to generate Paradox other times, then he should use the wolf-parts as a focus to cast healing effects, not make it an always-on thing.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4. What would you suggest for the mechanics of power like this? </div> </div> </div>Heal 1 Bashing/Lethal HL per turn. Pretty simple in effect. Probably needs 5-15 successes to establish if they're doing it as a permanent Pattern mod.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm also considering making him &quot;Wyrm Tainted.&quot; (It's mostly a Mage game, but there is significant interaction with Garou...) </div> </div> </div>Like a Skin Dancer? That is delicious.<br /> <br /> Note that other Mages might notice it too, if they have appropriate Spirit/Entropy senses up. It might be cleansable... but changing Resonance permanently <i>is</i> Prime 5... and Masters are in short supply these days. And if it's a Genetic Flaw, that's a Paradox Effect, so he'd have to swap in a different flaw.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm also thinking that if he wants to heal Ag damage, then it would cost Quintessence per health level... </div> </div> </div>Nah, wuffs don't heal Aggravated any faster than normal people. He obviously has the Life to heal it with a different Effect, which would naturally require 1 Q/Agg as usual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T22:15:51-07:00","id":972352,"title":"","content":"If you know what each Sphere does, it's easy to answer.<br /> <br /> To get &quot;Garou healing&quot;, you need Life 5 + Spirit 5 + Prime 4/5.<br /> <br /> Life 5 - because you're mutating your pattern, giving it new properties. Read about it in &quot;How do you DO that?&quot;, same way you can give someone innate abillity to breathe fire, teleport around, sidestep into Gauntlet (which is what Garou do), etcetera. Basically, giving innate abillities (like this regeneration) is Life 5.<br /> <br /> Now, Spirit 5 is shaping soul, molding it to your liking. Garou regeneration isn't only &quot;genetics&quot; or anything, it's a blessing from Gaia. You need to mold your soul to be blessed like that. After all, Garou are half spirits and have their own unique soul.<br /> <br /> Prime 4/5 is required to lock the Effect and possibly make you a travelling Wonder, or simply fuel the process thus avoid Pattern bleeding.<br /> <br /> You might even need Entropy 4/5. Entropy 4 is blessing physical Pattern, whereas Entropy 5 is capable of blessing the soul. Read above on why would you need to bless body and soul.<br /> <br /> It ain't easy, I know, but it's not supposed to be easy to give yourself blessing that was given to whole kind by Celestial.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12132-bogdan","name":"Bogdan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T00:57:44-07:00","id":972384,"title":"","content":"Alternatively there's the option to draw from the werewolf's heart's mystical some of the properties instead of mimicking ALL of it with your own magick (you still need to craft it like a talisman and thus you'd have need for appropriate Spheres if he's the one to craft it), which points me to say you're in luck, there's a layout for an already existing <i>talisman</i> that does something similar to what the character is trying to do; page 61 on Forged By Dragon's Fire. Only you could opt to use the heart other than the paw, on top of that it also offers a plethora of penalties like you intended him to offset the advantages.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://imgur.com/P09emLY\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://imgur.com/P09emLY\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://imgur.com/P09emLY\" target=\"_blank\"> http://imgur.com/P09emLY </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12152-rotwood","user":"Rotwood","date":". 09-19-2016, 04:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12152-rotwood","name":"Rotwood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T01:02:45-07:00","id":972386,"title":"","content":"Erm, what?<br /> <br /> By that standard, giving yourself scales is a Life 5/Prime 5/Entropy 5 effect. That's... absurd.<br /> <br /> Regeneration is just <i>healing really fast</i>. It should bloody well not require you to be a master of <i>four</i> Spheres to pull off, especially when two of those Spheres <i>aren't even contributing anything</i> to the effect. If you were giving yourself an Investment or Gift to regenerate, maybe, but Spirit isn't required to heal the body, and Entropy isn't required to make an Artifact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T01:12:33-07:00","id":972390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quantumboost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/972282-enhancing-yourself-to-heal-like-a-garou?p=972386#post972386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Erm, what?<br /> <br /> By that standard, giving yourself scales is a Life 5/Prime 5/Entropy 5 effect. That's... absurd.<br /> <br /> Regeneration is just <i>healing really fast</i>. It should bloody well not require you to be a master of <i>four</i> Spheres to pull off, especially when two of those Spheres <i>aren't even contributing anything</i> to the effect. If you were giving yourself an Investment or Gift to regenerate, maybe, but Spirit isn't required to heal the body, and Entropy isn't required to make an Artifact.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You clearly missunderstand.<br /> <br /> Giving yourself scales is changing appearance, tweaks to the body. Regeneration that works on it's own like for Garou - giving yourself innate abillities. That's completely different thing, and giving innate abillities is Life 5 according to &quot;How do you DO that?&quot;. If you want to use Golden Rule and make it different, sure then, but that's how Life Sphere works.<br /> <br /> Life 1 - percieve Life.<br /> Life 2 - heal self, minor tweaks.<br /> Life 3 - major tweaks but within human-size boundaries, healing others, damage, improvement.<br /> Life 4 - shapeshifting into animals that do not differ too much in size comparing to you, altering Attributes of others, short-death revival.<br /> Life 5 - full ressurection, giving new properties, major change in any organism, creating life.<br /> <br /> (This is very in a nutshell, Life sphere can do more of course)<br /> <br /> As for other Spheres, yes, they do contribute. Entropy corresponds to blessings, and that's exactly how Garou regeneration works. It's not just bunch of genetics, it's spiritual blessing, and through spiritual comes in Spirit Sphere.<br /> <br /> Though I agree on one thing, you might not need either Entropy or Spirit Sphere. Entropy deals with blessings as it was forementioned, and that's how Garou heal. Spirit Sphere, on the other hand, could help you in becoming exactly what Garou are, half spirits, to get closer to their state of regeneration.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, if you use only Life 5 to give yourself such property, I'm not sure it'd work so easily or correctly. It's a tricky deal, and wording it differently could make sense in many cases, not just one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12132-bogdan","name":"Bogdan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T01:13:20-07:00","id":972391,"title":"","content":"Yeah, there's not reason a mage needs to step outside of Life and Prime for this. Mimicking other supernaturals doesn't mean you have to add in other Spheres. You don't need Sphere to copy Garou powers unless the power involves something Spirit does. If you want to Mind control someone like a vampire, you don't need to add Matter to be more undead-like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T01:35:03-07:00","id":972398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Assume that something that\u2019s either conjured from raw<br /> energy or transmuted into a different form returns to its<br /> original state when the spell\u2019s duration passes. (See the<br /> Base Damage or Duration chart.) A \u201ctime-trigger\u201d (see<br /> Time 4) can set conditions around this reversal, and a<br /> large number of successes might make the transformation<br /> permanent. </div> </div> </div>&quot;How do you DO that?&quot; page 18. Why not just use Life and Time 4 - Time Trigger around a healing spell's reversal which will pretty much keep it in some sort of a loop and make it heal him constantly for a long time (Maybe permanently if he stacks up so many successes). He'll get paradox if he heals some .50 cal shot or smth though but yeah this should get the job done? (Sorry, I'm not the one to give opinions. Maybe I'm wrong who knows)<br /> But srsly, why try to be like a garou? is he trying to be sexy or trying some twilight shit? come on!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12133,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12133-leonardo","user":"Leonardo","date":". 09-19-2016, 04:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12133-leonardo","name":"Leonardo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T04:15:26-07:00","id":972447,"title":"","content":"Is no one going to talk about Pattern Bleed?<br /> <br /> This could undermine the whole thing since each enhancement will be giving him lethal damage for every day he keeps the effect active if it isn't made permanent.<br /> <br /> It could also be argued that pattern bleed cannot be healed with the effect that causes it, so he'd have to do a new life effect to deal with that each time.<br /> <br /> One more thing. The Permadox is going to add an extra layer of pain for this guy when it comes to mimicking a Garou if the Paradox storm is a thing in your game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T04:46:41-07:00","id":972451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leonardo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/972282-enhancing-yourself-to-heal-like-a-garou?p=972398#post972398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;How do you DO that?&quot; page 18. Why not just use Life and Time 4 - Time Trigger around a healing spell's reversal which will pretty much keep it in some sort of a loop and make it heal him constantly for a long time (Maybe permanently if he stacks up so many successes). He'll get paradox if he heals some .50 cal shot or smth though but yeah this should get the job done? (Sorry, I'm not the one to give opinions. Maybe I'm wrong who knows)<br /> But srsly, why try to be like a garou? is he trying to be sexy or trying some twilight shit? come on!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree, this could be more effective for &quot;burst healing&quot;. Though, you'd have to prepare many triggers and do them all the time, can get annoying.<br /> <br /> But that's for time trigger + healing. As for loop.. I don't think you can just &quot;loop&quot; healing spell and make it heal you constantly, considering also how powerful Life 3 looping can get. Even if it is somehow possible, there was discussion earlier about time triggers and Paradox, and it's been deducted that you'd get Paradox everytime upon the effect, not when you cast the ritual. So.. yeah, lots of Paradox to hit you.<br /> <br /> But then again, that sounds like twisting magick pretty badly. It's easier and safer to just stick to time triggers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is no one going to talk about Pattern Bleed?<br /> <br /> This could undermine the whole thing since each enhancement will be giving him lethal damage for every day he keeps the effect active if it isn't made permanent.<br /> <br /> It could also be argued that pattern bleed cannot be healed with the effect that causes it, so he'd have to do a new life effect to deal with that each time.<br /> <br /> One more thing. The Permadox is going to add an extra layer of pain for this guy when it comes to mimicking a Garou if the Paradox storm is a thing in your game. </div> </div> </div>Welp.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bogdan</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Prime 4/5 is required to lock the Effect and possibly make you a travelling Wonder, or simply fuel the process thus avoid Pattern bleeding.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd also agree that you cannot heal this damage. It's kind of silly if you use Life 5 to get that enchantment, get 1 Lethal per day, but you can just heal it back anyway with like 1 success. Makes Paradox absolutely toothless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12132-bogdan","name":"Bogdan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T05:43:00-07:00","id":972461,"title":"","content":"Speaking to flavor for a second - in the CoD Hunter game, there's a faction called the Cheiron Group that implants parts from monsters into its hunters to level the playing field (&quot;Thuamatechnology&quot;). One of them is sort of like this; they've found that werewolves often have &quot;knots&quot; where flesh has healed over on itself, and figured out how to implant them in a human. The hunter with one of these Regenerative Nodules can squeeze it and spend a Willpower to start healing a point of bashing a turn and a point of lethal every 15 minutes. To fuel it after use, they have to eat a hell of a lot of food or they take deprivation damage like they're starving.<br /> <br /> In that game, it's a four-dot Merit and not a &quot;castable&quot; thing, but that might give an idea how to roleplay this. Implant the werewolf heart in himself and hook it into all the normal veins and arteries. When he wants to heal, he starts up the werewolf heart and pumps blood through it for a while, then stops it when he's done. <br /> <br /> Mechanically you could still do whatever you want (implanted heart as a Wonder/Talisman that he fuels by injecting werewolf blood into the heart itself, implanted heart as a focus for somewhat less vulgar healing).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T08:24:37-07:00","id":972539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bogdan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/972282-enhancing-yourself-to-heal-like-a-garou?p=972390#post972390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You clearly missunderstand.<br /> <br /> Giving yourself scales is changing appearance, tweaks to the body. Regeneration that works on it's own like for Garou - giving yourself innate abillities. That's completely different thing, and giving innate abillities is Life 5 according to &quot;How do you DO that?&quot;. If you want to use Golden Rule and make it different, sure then, but that's how Life Sphere works.<br /> <br /> Life 1 - percieve Life.<br /> Life 2 - heal self, minor tweaks.<br /> Life 3 - major tweaks but within human-size boundaries, healing others, damage, improvement.<br /> Life 4 - shapeshifting into animals that do not differ too much in size comparing to you, altering Attributes of others, short-death revival.<br /> Life 5 - full ressurection, giving new properties, major change in any organism, creating life.<br /> <br /> (This is very in a nutshell, Life sphere can do more of course)<br /> <br /> As for other Spheres, yes, they do contribute. Entropy corresponds to blessings, and that's exactly how Garou regeneration works. It's not just bunch of genetics, it's spiritual blessing, and through spiritual comes in Spirit Sphere.<br /> <br /> Though I agree on one thing, you might not need either Entropy or Spirit Sphere. Entropy deals with blessings as it was forementioned, and that's how Garou heal. Spirit Sphere, on the other hand, could help you in becoming exactly what Garou are, half spirits, to get closer to their state of regeneration.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, if you use only Life 5 to give yourself such property, I'm not sure it'd work so easily or correctly. It's a tricky deal, and wording it differently could make sense in many cases, not just one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand perfectly.<br /> <br /> Giving yourself scales is adding a capability that's not in the human baseline. It can have mechanical effects, like bonus armor. Would you prefer I use gills as an example?<br /> <br /> You decided to include Prime as well. Prime can make things permanent effects when they wouldn't be otherwise, by way of creating Artifacts. If you need Prime 4, Life 5 shouldn't be necessary; the Spheres together can do <i>more things</i> than just the two individually, or earlier.<br /> <br /> Likewise, if you're using Prime to enchant/bless someone, you shouldn't need Entropy as well. 'Blessing' them is already part of the effect. How would it be different in any way if Entropy were absent? 'Garou stuff is a blessing not genetics' doesn't cut it, non-technomancers don't even <i>use</i> genetics.<br /> <br /> And like I said, unless you're mutilating your soul to imitate a spiritual Investment (complete with soul point loss), Spirit ain't doing shit. Maybe if you suggested they were fusing themselves to a Gaian spirit to make a Kami Mage, but that shouldn't require Prime or Entropy.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/972282-enhancing-yourself-to-heal-like-a-garou?p=972447#post972447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is no one going to talk about Pattern Bleed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pattern Bleed only matters if you're not embedding it into your True Pattern or making a Wonder. If they do make it a continuous but active effect, that would be a problem since magic can't heal the bleed damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6072,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","user":"Quantumboost","date":". 09-19-2016, 11:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T08:44:03-07:00","id":972546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I understand perfectly.<br /> <br /> Giving yourself scales is adding a capability that's not in the human baseline. It can have mechanical effects, like bonus armor. Would you prefer I use gills as an example?<br /> <br /> You decided to include Prime as well. Prime can make things permanent effects when they wouldn't be otherwise, by way of creating Artifacts. If you need Prime 4, Life 5 shouldn't be necessary; the Spheres together can do <i>more things</i> than just the two individually, or earlier.<br /> <br /> Likewise, if you're using Prime to enchant/bless someone, you shouldn't need Entropy as well. 'Blessing' them is already part of the effect. How would it be different in any way if Entropy were absent? 'Garou stuff is a blessing not genetics' doesn't cut it, non-technomancers don't even <i>use</i> genetics.<br /> <br /> And like I said, unless you're mutilating your soul to imitate a spiritual Investment (complete with soul point loss), Spirit ain't doing shit. Maybe if you suggested they were fusing themselves to a Gaian spirit to make a Kami Mage, but that shouldn't require Prime or Entropy. </div> </div> </div>That ain't innate abillity though, you're wording it wrong.<br /> <br /> Giving yourself scales, and body armor (which is actually mentioned in mage books) is Life 3. That's pretty much getting bonus dice.<br /> <br /> Innate abillity is something more like what I already mentioned. Fire breath, abillity to teleport around, etcetera.<br /> <br /> As for Prime being involved, that's to avoid Pattern bleed. Entropy corresponds to blessings, and then again we're back to the fact that some would percieve Garou regeneration as blessing through their paradigm, thus require it. Same about Spirit, as per chapter &quot;Little bit of Spirit?&quot; in M20 when a mage is capable of adding Spirit Sphere into his workings.<br /> <br /> It's up to you as Storyteller what you want to do, really, and how much you &quot;value&quot; that Gaian blessing. Do you want it to be just a matter of innate abillity to regenerate? Go on with that Life 5 and Prime 4. You're making it a blessing? Go on with that Entropy. You make your spirit similar to Garou's? Yeah, guess what Sphere you'd pick then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12132-bogdan","name":"Bogdan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T09:19:21-07:00","id":972565,"title":"","content":"Restoring health levels is an innate ability humans already have. Just like soaking damage. All this does is amplify and improve that.<br /> <br /> You don't need Prime to avoid Pattern Bleed, Life can do that all by itself, per Verbena Revised.<br /> <br /> My issue is, you are advising an ST - which means &quot;ST's call&quot; is just a way of justifying irresponsibility - to add in Master-level Spheres that don't actually contribute to what the player seems to want to do. &quot;I want to heal fast&quot; does not require &quot;I want to have a fate-binding and mutilate my soul to seem more Werewolfish&quot;. That's also the same bullshit that makes HDYDT Horizon Realms outside the range of any Traditions Mage who's ever lived.<br /> <br /> You want to spend soul points instead of experience, like you were getting a spirit Investment? Sure, Spirit 5, maybe with Life - or maybe not. Fuse with a Gaian spirit to take it as a Charm? Spirit 4/Life 4, possibly 5 depending on how deep the fusion needs to be. Blessing yourself with rapid healing? Life/Entropy 4. Infusing yourself with raw power to enchant your body to heal faster? Life/Prime 4. Alter your body to simply restore itself periodically? Life 5.<br /> <br /> There are multiple ways to do a given thing in Mage, and you are choosing to require <i>all</i> of them, not just one of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6072,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","user":"Quantumboost","date":". 09-19-2016, 12:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T10:05:45-07:00","id":972581,"title":"","content":"Developmental Neogenetics Amalgamated, is trying to achieve the same thing, thinking they could benefit all of humanity if you want a crossover idea, they could be working with technocrats to do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T05:52:54-07:00","id":973779,"title":"","content":"&quot;Heal Like a Garou&quot;<br /> <br /> ...Why? That's a horrible idea. Paradox would be a bitch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T19:29:46-07:00","id":993251,"title":"","content":"1) Life 5 with Permanent Paradox and maybe Pattern Bleeding.<br /> 2) Life 3/Time 4. Some of your successes are a &quot;bank&quot; of healing and when you are injured, that's the conditional trigger that makes a withdrawal of 1 success per to HL healed. You are subject to Unbelief if you heal serious lethal or any aggravated damage.<br /> 3) Turn yourself into a &quot;relic&quot; with Life and Prime. You heal, but it costs Quintessence.<br /> 4) Just use Life on yourself when you need it and stop making things excessively complicated for yourself.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":164,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","user":"Malcolm","date":". 10-27-2016, 11:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T19:19:38-07:00","id":993837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/972282-enhancing-yourself-to-heal-like-a-garou?p=972581#post972581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Developmental Neogenetics Amalgamated, is trying to achieve the same thing, thinking they could benefit all of humanity if you want a crossover idea, they could be working with technocrats to do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>And banging their heads on the wall because they just can't isolate what's providing such wondrous vitality, even after so much time and funding have been spent to do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T09:51:17-07:00","id":994084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gabryl</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/972282-enhancing-yourself-to-heal-like-a-garou#post972282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to see how some of y'all would handle this from a player:<br /> <br /> He would like to, through Sphere magick, give his character the ability to regenerate damage &quot;like a werewolf.&quot;<br /> <br /> He has Life 4, Spirit 3, Prime 4.<br /> <br /> He has taken the heart from a garou and has been using it in his sanctum to try to figure some things out. He's come up with the idea of giving himself a second heart and he wants the following effect:<br /> <br /> Whenever hurt, heal one health level per round. (He also wants (eventually) to gain the &quot;revive recently dead&quot; power).<br /> <br /> Specific Questions:<br /> 1. What are the sphere effects you'd require for the above power?<br /> 2. Would you use the &quot;enhancement&quot; background to cover this (representing permanent modification to his pattern)?<br /> 3. Player is trying to argue that he shouldn't get permanent paradox, but instead it should generate paradox when healing...<br /> 4. What would you suggest for the mechanics of power like this?<br /> <br /> My take so far:<br /> <br /> I'm inclined to let the player do this, if only because I think it's a horrible idea. I told him we'd work on things... but I'm assuming that we'll start with creating a wonder and then making it a permanent change in his pattern.... (to figure out costs). I think this should then be handled through the Enhancement Background.<br /> <br /> It feels like, maybe, this power should require Time 4 as well... so that it only heals him when he's hurt...<br /> <br /> I'm considering letting him take Genetic Flaws instead of the Permadox. (I really don't like the idea of having this sort of power without a significant price (and not just in a dangerously difficult casting...)<br /> <br /> I'm also considering making him &quot;Wyrm Tainted.&quot; (It's mostly a Mage game, but there is significant interaction with Garou...)<br /> <br /> I'm also thinking that if he wants to heal Ag damage, then it would cost Quintessence per health level...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Concerning the Wyrm tainted, don't you think it should be Wyld ? I mean... this Mage is trying to still from Gaia gifts to the Garou ? Main consequence could be that every spirit will pursue him for that insult...<br /> <br /> Concerning the intial question, I would go for :<br /> - Life 3 with healing over time instead of amount of healed points. This, way, the Mage would heal one lethal a round until the spell lasts,<br /> - Or, the Mage could go to Life 4 to make a permanent change to his pattern, but he would endure Pattern bleeding,<br /> - In the end, he could go for Life 5 and definitely change his pattern. This would solve the pattern bleeding problem.<br /> <br /> For the last two solutions, permadox can not be avoided (and should not), and it would require a large amount of successes. But as for the first solution, I see no problem with either paradox nor need for quintessence in the case he just wants to heal lethal. In any case, the Mage should earn specific Resonnance for this (and as implied above, I would go for Dynamic resonnance).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T19:31:14-07:00","id":994349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NicoTheDuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/972282-enhancing-yourself-to-heal-like-a-garou?p=994084#post994084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Concerning the Wyrm tainted, don't you think it should be Wyld ? I mean... this Mage is trying to still from Gaia gifts to the Garou ? Main consequence could be that every spirit will pursue him for that insult...</div> </div> </div> </div>The Wyld is not Gaia. The Wyld is also not your friend, or anyone else's. Not even the Ratkin, who have spent too much time around it and ended up unhinged from the experience. The reason that Garou and Fera might fight to preserve manifestations of it is because it's not the Weaver or Wyrm, not because of an inherent connection or friendship. The Wyld simply is, and channeling its power instead of the Wyrm's can often end up with the same messy result. Just look at how many powers gorgons share with fomori in Possessed.<br /> <br /> Not that any given mage is likely to be well-versed in anything Triatic. It tends to sneak by them, and they aren't usually looking for it, or particularly comprehending of what it is even if they're looking right at it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T00:51:22-07:00","id":994454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/972282-enhancing-yourself-to-heal-like-a-garou?p=994349#post994349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not that any given mage is likely to be well-versed in anything Triatic. It tends to sneak by them, and they aren't usually looking for it, or particularly comprehending of what it is even if they're looking right at it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless the game you're running is Mage, in which case the Weaver, Wyld, and Wyrm are just the Garou's weird name for the trinity of Stasis, Dynamism, and Entropy. And that the werewolves are just projecting all-powerful importance on entities that are just three of many Umbral entities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T03:23:13-07:00","id":994480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/972282-enhancing-yourself-to-heal-like-a-garou?p=994454#post994454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless the game you're running is Mage, in which case the Weaver, Wyld, and Wyrm are just the Garou's weird name for the trinity of Stasis, Dynamism, and Entropy. And that the werewolves are just projecting all-powerful importance on entities that are just three of many Umbral entities.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never understadood it as wierd names for the metaphysical trinity. I mean... I think you can even meet the Wyrm in the Umbra (it's at least suggested in Penny Dreadful, but ok, this a novel...). Don't you think the Triat is more or less the spiritual representation of the metaphysical trinity ? As the trinity exists in concepts, it should be embodied in some way by spirits. Well, that's a way to view things that I find interesting, but I lack information on the Garou (just played it once with friends) no little about their setting and story. I might be mistaken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T10:40:44-07:00","id":994663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NicoTheDuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/972282-enhancing-yourself-to-heal-like-a-garou?p=994480#post994480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I never understadood it as wierd names for the metaphysical trinity. I mean... I think you can even meet the Wyrm in the Umbra (it's at least suggested in Penny Dreadful, but ok, this a novel...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Firstly, novels have included an imbued getting knocked up by a metis Garou. Secondly, meeting the Wyrm, the whole, actual Wyrm, would be an experience that would break the mind, because it's a spirit with a maw vast enough to consume galaxies. Malfeas, a Realm in the Deep Umbra, is where it's trapped, but this does not make the whole Supernal easily accessed by any means. That would be counter to the wishes of all of the sad, broken entities that exist as a part of the trapped Wyrm, which would cease to exist in short order if it were to become free. Expect heavy resistance from the Triatic Wyrms, which, though mere gnawing madness in the Wyrm's mind, are ranked as Celestines.<br /> <br /> Also, the better question would be why Mage keeps sticking to a metaphysical trinity, because the Triat came first. Mage was released a year after Werewolf, recall.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> . Don't you think the Triat is more or less the spiritual representation of the metaphysical trinity ? As the trinity exists in concepts, it should be embodied in some way by spirits. Well, that's a way to view things that I find interesting, but I lack information on the Garou (just played it once with friends) no little about their setting and story. I might be mistaken. </div> </div> </div>Mage didn't have to be a hot mess of Ars Magica Modern trying to link itself up to a greater WoD, and things would probably not be such a horrid, tangled, contentious mess if Mage had actually had its own playground. The metaphysical trinity is perhaps the greatest representation of a failed crossover attempt built right into a game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T13:54:36-07:00","id":995794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/972282-enhancing-yourself-to-heal-like-a-garou?p=994663#post994663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage didn't have to be a hot mess of Ars Magica Modern trying to link itself up to a greater WoD, and things would probably not be such a horrid, tangled, contentious mess if Mage had actually had its own playground. The metaphysical trinity is perhaps the greatest representation of a failed crossover attempt built right into a game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree but that's your opinion. Anyway, I was just wandering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}